WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:03.040
october

00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:10.639
i'm gonna head your way
and see you today

00:00:11.599 --> 00:00:18.320
though sometimes i wonder why i should

00:00:19.680 --> 00:00:23.439
sometimes you don't seem to care

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:28.480
and that makes me mad brother

00:00:29.439 --> 00:00:36.160
and then when i see you it doesn't
really make me feel any better

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:40.399
should it

00:00:41.360 --> 00:00:45.840
is that what this is for

00:00:46.719 --> 00:00:49.760
it doesn't seem to be

00:00:50.719 --> 00:00:58.239
it actually just makes me remember the
way things used to be

00:00:58.239 --> 00:01:00.960
better times

00:01:02.480 --> 00:01:07.600
it makes me wonder why things turned out
this way

00:01:08.960 --> 00:01:18.240
what did i do wrong
should i have done something different

00:01:19.439 --> 00:01:22.400
what could i have said

00:01:25.520 --> 00:01:30.560
you never let me down ever

00:01:32.640 --> 00:01:36.560
but now you won't even talk to me

00:01:38.960 --> 00:01:44.000
i was looking at some of the things you
wrote to me in the past

00:01:44.720 --> 00:01:47.920
i opened up an email

00:01:49.280 --> 00:01:55.840
in it you wrote i feel it again
washing over me

00:01:55.840 --> 00:01:59.840
the descent into degeneration and
disintegration

00:01:59.840 --> 00:02:08.319
the smell of filth black water mixed
with blood and gun powder and shit

00:02:08.319 --> 00:02:16.480
the american soldier covered in filth
11 months into a 16-month deployment

00:02:18.080 --> 00:02:25.520
the insurgents grown
men hiding behind children

00:02:25.840 --> 00:02:32.160
women wailing over the dead explosions
and screams and fragments of concrete

00:02:32.160 --> 00:02:40.480
flying through the air
and frogmen enter the scene to take the

00:02:40.480 --> 00:02:46.000
hand of the american soldier
and pull him from the whirlpool

00:02:46.000 --> 00:02:51.840
to set his feet back on the rock and
speak words of hope

00:02:52.959 --> 00:02:57.120
we are the prophets of doom and
destruction we enter an area

00:02:57.120 --> 00:03:01.760
and take back the lost pride of america

00:03:02.319 --> 00:03:07.680
we redden the stripes blew the field
and make the stars of our tattered and

00:03:07.680 --> 00:03:13.120
humiliated battle ensign
shine once again

00:03:14.480 --> 00:03:19.760
we hold it high we carry a nation on our
shoulders

00:03:19.760 --> 00:03:23.840
and we bring the enemy to its knees

00:03:25.519 --> 00:03:28.560
we do not live in fear of death or
wounding

00:03:28.560 --> 00:03:33.840
or even worse rejection by the country
we love

00:03:36.080 --> 00:03:42.959
i feel my mind coming apart and the old
sleeping animal coming out

00:03:43.840 --> 00:03:48.400
i tried to keep it inside but it cannot
help

00:03:48.400 --> 00:03:53.360
but attend the call to battle

00:03:59.760 --> 00:04:06.560
when you originally wrote that to me
i thought to myself

00:04:06.560 --> 00:04:11.920
yep he's there again

00:04:13.040 --> 00:04:15.840
where he should be

00:04:17.280 --> 00:04:20.959
i knew it wouldn't last forever

00:04:22.960 --> 00:04:26.000
but where are you now

00:04:27.680 --> 00:04:30.880
now you seem distant

00:04:31.680 --> 00:04:36.880
in my head i can see you smile i can
hear you laugh

00:04:36.880 --> 00:04:45.199
but it's only in my head
i was surfing the other day it was one

00:04:45.199 --> 00:04:51.440
of those days
a good day solid swell

00:04:51.440 --> 00:04:57.840
no wind tide was low and the sky was
clear and bright

00:05:00.400 --> 00:05:07.759
i kept looking out toward the outside
where you used to sit and wait for the

00:05:07.759 --> 00:05:11.840
big set waves

00:05:12.479 --> 00:05:16.080
i thought i saw you a couple times

00:05:17.039 --> 00:05:19.840
but it wasn't you

00:05:20.960 --> 00:05:28.639
i heard someone paddling behind me
must be you i thought

00:05:29.360 --> 00:05:34.160
no nothing

00:05:34.479 --> 00:05:41.280
no one's there
i'm all alone out here

00:05:44.240 --> 00:05:48.880
everything is the same but nothing is
the same

00:05:49.520 --> 00:05:53.840
everything has changed but nothing has
changed

00:05:56.240 --> 00:05:59.600
does anything ever change

00:06:01.520 --> 00:06:07.600
look at the waves as they approach the
shore

00:06:07.600 --> 00:06:13.600
each wave formed through random
combinations of wind and sea and

00:06:13.600 --> 00:06:20.479
pressure
and each one completely unique

00:06:20.479 --> 00:06:26.319
and when they break they're gone forever

00:06:29.120 --> 00:06:35.840
but then another one comes behind it
and another one

00:06:36.479 --> 00:06:39.520
they are all different

00:06:40.560 --> 00:06:43.600
but they're all the same

00:06:44.880 --> 00:06:48.319
and i see some of the past and the
future and i see some of the future in

00:06:48.319 --> 00:06:54.400
the past
and i begin to wonder which is which

00:06:56.240 --> 00:06:59.280
how did i get here

00:07:01.039 --> 00:07:04.400
where am i going to end up

00:07:06.639 --> 00:07:09.280
where are you

00:07:11.680 --> 00:07:18.800
i look at some more of your writing
you are telling a story writing a story

00:07:18.800 --> 00:07:30.240
about a man about god
about life about death

00:07:30.240 --> 00:07:33.440
and this is what you wrote

00:07:34.319 --> 00:07:39.440
i am ready to go he thought to himself

00:07:39.919 --> 00:07:45.520
but for you i wait for the appointed
time

00:07:45.520 --> 00:07:51.199
thy will he said to himself
and closed his eyes and placed his hands

00:07:51.199 --> 00:07:54.720
on the pages
as if there was some strength there and

00:07:54.720 --> 00:08:03.039
he prayed
while he prayed he also thought of past

00:08:03.039 --> 00:08:05.520
times

00:08:06.240 --> 00:08:16.560
he breathed in deep and exhaled
deliver us from the evil one he muttered

00:08:17.039 --> 00:08:22.639
and he thought of all the reasons he had
no right to say this prayer

00:08:24.400 --> 00:08:30.800
at that he steadied himself
opened his eyes and looked out into the

00:08:30.800 --> 00:08:36.080
first light of the morning
he saw a face not his own looking back

00:08:36.080 --> 00:08:40.800
at him from the window
and disappeared

00:08:40.800 --> 00:08:44.000
but he was not startled

00:08:44.240 --> 00:08:48.080
this kind of thing was normal

00:08:48.959 --> 00:08:56.560
i'm ready for you he thought to himself
while he ran that morning he did not

00:08:56.560 --> 00:09:02.240
think about anything
his mind retreated deep into itself or

00:09:02.240 --> 00:09:04.640
perhaps it shut down altogether and he
wore

00:09:04.640 --> 00:09:09.600
no expression he only looked out at the
sea

00:09:09.600 --> 00:09:14.320
and watched as the seabirds glided above
the undulating plane of water

00:09:14.320 --> 00:09:18.399
moving close above its surface but
managing somehow

00:09:18.399 --> 00:09:24.720
not to touch it
at home he heaved weights around on a

00:09:24.720 --> 00:09:29.040
small
concrete slab his routine

00:09:29.040 --> 00:09:32.080
effortlessly recited and at the same
time

00:09:32.080 --> 00:09:39.360
painfully undertaken again
without thought or care

00:09:40.080 --> 00:09:43.200
every morning the same

00:09:43.360 --> 00:09:48.080
marking off time until an appointed end

00:09:48.240 --> 00:09:51.839
his final rendezvous

00:09:56.480 --> 00:09:59.360
that's what you wrote

00:10:02.160 --> 00:10:06.640
is that what we are doing here marking
off time

00:10:06.640 --> 00:10:09.760
until an appointed end

00:10:12.320 --> 00:10:23.360
my memory plays tricks on me
how many days do i remember

00:10:23.760 --> 00:10:28.959
how many days do i actually remember

00:10:31.040 --> 00:10:36.079
and what good is a day that i can't
remember

00:10:37.360 --> 00:10:40.000
did it happen

00:10:40.399 --> 00:10:43.200
did it exist

00:10:44.880 --> 00:10:49.760
i want to remember every day but i can't

00:10:52.480 --> 00:10:55.600
i let some of them go

00:10:56.240 --> 00:11:02.640
and i hate that
i want to remember and re-remember the

00:11:02.640 --> 00:11:06.560
times
we had together

00:11:12.959 --> 00:11:16.800
we played songs on the guitar

00:11:18.560 --> 00:11:22.320
but i can't hear them anymore

00:11:24.399 --> 00:11:33.920
they are gone
i can't recreate them

00:11:35.920 --> 00:11:38.800
i'm not good enough

00:11:41.440 --> 00:11:45.839
